# Delimited fence highlighting

## Root cause

The theme receives Carve code blocks as Markdown fences and asks Pygments for the named language. CSV and TSV fences reach that path, but the plugin does not depend on a package that registers either lexer.

## Change

Require the first pygments-carve release with CSV and TSV entry points. Send TSV source directly to Pymdownx Highlight before Python-Markdown expands its tabs, while CSV keeps the normal Markdown fence path. Exercise both languages in a real Zensical build and check the separator scope.

## Scope

The dependency makes the registered lexers available to every site using this plugin. The TSV path applies to every TSV fence, including titled blocks, because Python-Markdown expands all tab characters before fence highlighting.
